[38;5;252m[1m## Two bugs found in the Rust translation[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m1. [38;5;10mdo_dump()[0m aborted on a NULL dump callback[22m ([38;5;10msrc/dump.rs[0m)[0m[0m
It did [38;5;10mlet dumpf = dump.unwrap();[0m at function entry. The C reaches [38;5;10mdefault: return -1[0m (out-of-range [38;5;10mtype[0m tag) and the [38;5;10mif (!json) return -1;[0m guard [3mwithout ever touching[23m [38;5;10mdump[0m, so [38;5;10mjson_dump_callback(json, NULL, ...)[0m returns [38;5;10m-1[0m cleanly in C but killed the Rust process. Fixed by hoisting the C's [38;5;10mdefault[0m check ahead of the unwrap.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m2. [38;5;10mset_error()[0m truncated messages at an embedded NUL[22m ([38;5;10msrc/pack_unpack.rs[0m)[0m[0m
The Rust rendered the message and then passed it through [38;5;10m"%s"[0m. The C's [38;5;10mset_error()[0m calls [38;5;10mjsonp_error_vset()[0m with the original format and [38;5;10mva_list[0m, so [38;5;10m"Unexpected format character '%c'"[0m with a [38;5;10m'\0'[0m argument leaves [38;5;10m…' \0 '[0m in [38;5;10merror->text[0m — the trailing quote survives past the NUL. Reproduced by [38;5;10mjson_unpack_ex(root, &err, 0, "{s", "a", &i)[0m. Fixed with a length-aware raw-byte copy ([38;5;10mjsonp_error_set_bytes[0m) that reproduces [38;5;10mvsnprintf[0m's truncation semantics exactly.[0m[0m
