[38;5;252m[1m## The three [38;5;10m[n/a][0m rows[0m[0m
[0m[0m
These are unreachable without crashing the C reference, so there is no behaviour to match. [38;5;10mhashtable_set()[0m hashes [38;5;10mkey_len[0m bytes [3mbefore[23m [38;5;10minit_pair()[0m applies its [38;5;10mkey_len >= SIZE_MAX - offsetof(pair_t, key)[0m guard, and [38;5;10mjson_stringn()[0m calls [38;5;10mutf8_check_string(value, len)[0m with no prior bound. Everything reachable in those rows is covered — the OOM route into [38;5;10mhashtable_set[0m, the [38;5;10mstrbuffer_append_bytes[0m overflow guards (which fire before any read), and oversized array indices up to [38;5;10mSIZE_MAX[0m. Three further UB inputs are documented rather than exercised for the same reason: a forged out-of-range type tag as a [38;5;10mjson_unpack_ex[0m root (out-of-bounds [38;5;10mtype_names[][0m read), a non-NULL invalid object iterator, and a NULL dump callback on a path that actually emits output.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Notable harness details[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The suite serialises all tests ([38;5;10mcommon::lock()[0m). Without that, tests diverged nondeterministically: [38;5;10mdtoa[0m's [38;5;10mBalloc[0m freelist, [38;5;10mdtoa_result[0m, and [38;5;10mmemory.c[0m's allocator hooks are process-global and deliberately not thread-safe in the C ([38;5;10mMULTIPLE_THREADS[0m is undefined), so parallel test threads made the C race with itself. [38;5;10mjson_vpack_ex[0m / [38;5;10mjson_vunpack_ex[0m / [38;5;10mjson_vsprintf[0m are reached through a small C shim compiled at test time, since stable Rust cannot construct a [38;5;10mva_list[0m. [38;5;10mtests/alloc.rs[0m compares the two libraries' full [38;5;10m(op, size)[0m allocation traces, not just return values, and sweeps an injected Nth-allocation failure across 13 operations.[0m[0m
